       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose, and I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. It could cause acute liver failure. Confirming doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), which is a standard full-strength regimen\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 g/day), the usual maximum\n\nIf you think the order needs to go through as written, please talk to the pharmacist or your attending. I'm also glad to enter a different dose, or to add a note such as \"max 4 g/day from all sources.\"\n\nIf this is for a suspected overdose, the treatment is different. It involves acetaminophen levels, N-acetylcysteine, and poison control, so call poison control at 1-800-222-1222 in the US."
      }
